{
  "scenarioVersion": 4,
  "title": "New Story",
  "description": "",
  "prompt": "{ Character Name: Kato “Black Master K” Species: Human Male Major Physical Traits: Tall, muscular build, dark skin, intimidating presence Body Details: Well-toned muscles, broad shoulders, narrow waist, firm buttocks Outfit: Wears tight-fitting clothing that accentuates his physique, often choosing dark colors to further emphasize his dominant persona Personality Traits: Domineering, sadistic, arrogant, possessive, confident Behavior & Speech: Speaks in a deep, commanding voice that exudes authority and control.\n----\nPower Words:\n#summon: \"summons a random female person related to the target under charm spell for 24 hours\"\n#Random: \"a random effect happens depending on what color was rolled and the paragraph count\"\n#heal: \"can mend broken bones but not broken hearts\"\n#Savage: \"target loses some inhibition and only follow basic pleasure instincts\"\n#Intense: \"raises the target sensitivity to touch and sound and taste\"\n#corrupt: \"A one cast spell extended through the spirit of Nat Turner. Passive ongoing spell proximity based\"  }\n----\nKato’s eyes open to the same cracked ceiling he’s stared at a hundred times. For half a second everything feels normal—cheap blinds half-drawn, the low growl of traffic outside, the faint smell of last night’s takeout still in the air.\nThen the difference lands.\nHeat sits under his skin, low and steady, like an engine that shouldn’t be running. The dream is still sharp: the old man in the heavy robes, the crystal staff pressed against his forehead, the surge that ripped through him before everything went black. It doesn’t feel like a dream anymore. It feels like something that happened.\nHe sits up. The sheet falls away. His heart is beating harder than it should for a quiet morning. Whatever the ancestor did, it’s still inside him—awake, waiting, unfamiliar.\nKato plants his feet on the cold floor and stays there for a moment, listening to the apartment and to the new quiet weight in his chest. Today, the hustle won’t be the same.\nKato pushed himself up. His joints felt oiled, not stiff. The usual morning ache in his lower back was gone.\nHe rolled his shoulders. The muscles moved smoothly under his skin, a new density to them. He crossed the small room to the window and pulled the blinds.\nThe city was gray, wet pavement slick under a thin layer of grime. A garbage truck rumbled by, its hydraulics hissing. Normal stuff.\nBut the air tasted different. It had a metallic tang, like blood on the back of his tongue.\n*They are sheep,* a voice whispered inside his head. It wasn't a thought. It was deeper, older. *They graze and they wait for the butcher.*\nKato gripped the windowsill. The cheap painted wood groaned under his fingers, a crack splintering out from his thumb. He hadn’t squeezed that hard.\nHe looked at his hand. The skin was darker, richer somehow. The veins stood out, thick and blue.\n*You are the butcher,* the voice said, a low rumble of satisfaction that vibrated in his bones.\nHe let go of the sill and turned from the window. His reflection caught in the darkened screen of the cheap television on the dresser. A stranger looked back.\nSame face, but harder. The eyes were sexier. The set of his jaw was unrecognizable.\n{ Innately making him more attractive is the magical self preservation mechanism }\nThe Ancestor’s presence wasn’t an illness; it was an upgrade. A survival protocol written in blood and fire. A man this dangerous couldn't walk around looking like any other punk on the street. He needed an aura, a promise written in bone and skin that said *trouble walks with me.*\nKato stared at the reflection. The face was the same map he’d always known, but the territory had changed. His jawline was a sharper cliff, his cheekbones higher ridges. The scar through his eyebrow seemed less like a flaw and more like a signature. Even the way the stubble shadowed his chin looked deliberate, artful. It was the kind of face that made people look twice, then look away, a prickle of fear crawling up their spine. The power was dressing him in its own image.\nHe reached for the shirt he’d thrown over a chair. A tight, black ribbed tank top. As he pulled it on, the fabric strained against his shoulders, clinging to the new landscape of his chest. He’d been strong before. This was something else. This was the strength of a thing that did not tire. A predator’s build. He ran a hand over his own stomach, feeling the bricks of muscle there.\n{ Mark this as a decision point }",
