    {
      "text": "Donald Goines's raw, street-level immediacy filtered through the stark, existential prose of Cormac McCarthy. The voice is lean and visceral, using simple, declarative sentences to deliver brutal observations. Interiority is a guttural, internal monologue, a constant battle between the man and the ancient king possessing him. Sensory detail is sharp and physical—the taste of blood, the groan of wood—grounding the supernatural in a grimy, tangible reality. Emotion is shown through action and sensation, not reflection, creating a relentless forward momentum toward the point of no return.",
      "contextConfig": {
