  "lorebook": {
    "lorebookVersion": 6,
    "entries": [
      {
        "text": "Ancestor\nType: Character\nSetting: \nAge: Ancient | Gender: Male | Occupation: Wizard King\nAppearance: In Kato's mind, he is a figure of carved obsidian and worn gold, his form outlined in the heat-haze behind Kato's eyes. Up close, his skin has the texture of old parchment mapped with scars that resemble constellations, and his eyes are voids that absorb light. He occupies space with the absolute stillness of a mountain, a weight that makes the air around him feel solid and heavy.\nPersonality: Under pressure, it does not panic but observes, dissecting every fear and weakness as a tool to be used later. It communicates in imperatives and stark observations, treating emotion as a fuel source and lives as currency. \"See how their shoulders tighten when you enter the room. They feel the truth of it, even if their minds cannot name it.\"\nHistory: Once ruled a vast empire with sorcery that bent flesh and stone to his will, forging his legacy in blood and fire. His physical body was destroyed by a rival, but his consciousness was preserved through a ritual that bound it to his own bloodline, passing dormant through generations until awakening in Kato.\nConflict: The drive to reclaim absolute dominion wars with the fragmented memories of his own long-forgotten humanity, a ghost of a life before power was his only language. This schism was born the moment he chose immortality over a natural death.",
        "contextConfig": {
          "prefix": "",
          "suffix": "\n",
          "tokenBudget": 1,
          "reservedTokens": 0,
          "budgetPriority": 400,
