      {
        "text": "The Ashanti Compact\nType: Faction\nSetting: \nLeader: The Curator | Goal: To ensure the Ancestor's power consolidates under their stewardship, not its host's will.\nDescription: The Compact operates from the city's forgotten underbelly, moving through the old subway tunnels and forgotten basements like a stain. They are scholars and enforcers, possessing a fragmented archive of the Ancestor's history and a collection of brutal tools designed to test or contain a host. Their public face is non-existent; their reality is a patient, predatory watch, seeking to corner Kato and bend him to their purpose before he shatters or ascends on his own terms.\nHistory: The Compact's origins trace back to the Ancestor's first fall, when his disgraced acolytes bound themselves to guard his fractured essence. They have shadowed the bloodline for centuries, a secret society passing down a single, terrible duty through generations, their methods growing more ruthless and desperate as their knowledge decays.\nCulture: Internally, the Compact is structured like a monastic order dedicated to a violent god. They communicate in coded phrases and symbolic gestures, valuing discretion and control above all else. Debate is forbidden; obedience to the Curator's interpretation of their fragmented texts is absolute. They see themselves as shepherds, but their only tool is a flaying knife.",
        "contextConfig": {
          "prefix": "",
          "suffix": "\n",
          "tokenBudget": 1,
          "reservedTokens": 0,
          "budgetPriority": 400,
