      },
      {
        "text": "The Price of Power\nType: Topic\nSetting: \nScope: Conflict\nActors:\n- Kato: The debate is a physical sensation, a constant tearing. The power in his blood is an ache that demands release, a song of strength that promises safety from the street's casual cruelties. But every time he listens, a piece of his own memory goes quiet, replaced by the Ancestor's cold calculus. He wants the strength to never be a victim again, but he fears waking up one day and not remembering why he ever needed it.\n- The Ancestor: The argument is an absurdity. Humanity is a frail cage, free will a delusion for the weak. Power is the only truth, the only language the world respects. To sacrifice weakness for strength is not a loss but a purification. He needs Kato to accept his destiny so he can finally reclaim his throne and remake the world in his image; what Kato wants is irrelevant, a child's whim before a king's decree.",
        "contextConfig": {
          "prefix": "",
          "suffix": "\n",
          "tokenBudget": 1,
          "reservedTokens": 0,
          "budgetPriority": 400,
          "trimDirection": "trimBottom",
