      {
        "text": "Human, 46, Potential WIzard King\n\nI control the power. The power does not control me.\n\nEyes are the first thing you notice—pitch-black, no discernible iris or pupil. They absorb light. Skin is the color of polished obsidian, unblemished. Close-cropped hair frames a strong, square jaw. Muscles are dense and clearly defined, layered over a broad-shouldered, narrow-waisted frame. He stands with a predatory stillness, weight distributed evenly. A thin, pale scar cuts through his left eyebrow, interrupting the dark symmetry of his face. The knuckles on his right hand are enlarged, scarred from repeated impact.\n\nKato speaks in a measured, deliberate cadence. It’s a rhythmic, persuasive flow, reminiscent of African-American Vernacular English (AAVE), often dropping final consonants from words like \"jus'\" for \"just.\" His signature habit is a slow, deliberate blink, holding his eyes shut for a beat longer than normal, as if processing a thought the world isn't ready for. He moves with a contained stillness, power held in reserve.\n\nCore driver is the need to dominate. He believes control is the only defense against powerlessness. The wound is a deep-seated fear of being weak, of being the sheep he despises. This contradiction fuels him: he seeks absolute power, yet is terrified of the power he wields, convinced it is a separate entity that could consume him. He controls the power to prove he is not its slave, even as its voice dictates his actions.",
        "contextConfig": {
          "prefix": "",
          "suffix": "\n",
          "tokenBudget": 1,
          "reservedTokens": 0,
          "budgetPriority": 400,
